{#- FAQ accordion + FAQPage structured data, generated from the SAME entries
    (src/_data/faq.js) so the visible copy and the schema can never disagree
    — Google treats a mismatch between them as a structured-data violation.

    Built with native <details>/<summary> on purpose: the answer text sits in
    the DOM whether or not the panel is open, so crawlers and AI fetchers
    that never run JavaScript still read every answer. Do not swap this for
    a JS-driven accordion that injects or removes the answers — that is
    exactly the content an answer engine comes for.

    The first item ships open so the section reads as answers, not a row of
    closed bars.

    Ground: sits between reserve/visit and newsletter/contact in the default
    homepage order (src/index.njk). `reviews` (src/_data/reviews.js) is off
    by default, so the usual neighbour above is visit (white) and this ground
    is secondary-50; a build that also turns on client.reviews gets
    visit -> reviews (secondary-50) -> faq, so the ground flips to white to
    still alternate. Re-check this against its actual neighbours if a build
    also turns visit or newsletter off — same rule as any other section
    (CLAUDE.md, "Removing a section means re-deriving the grounds"). -#}
{% if faq and faq.length %}
{%- set faqGround = 'bg-white' if (reviews and reviews.items.length) else 'bg-secondary-50' %}
<section id="faq" class="section {{ faqGround }}">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal="up">
      <p class="eyebrow">Good to Know</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl divide-y divide-gray-200 border-t border-b border-gray-200" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="1">
      {% for item in faq %}
      <details class="group py-6" {% if loop.first %}open{% endif %}>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">{{ item.question }}</h3>
          <svg class="size-5 flex-shrink-0 text-accent-500 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8 2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v4.5h4.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4.5v4.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-4.5h-4.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h4.5v-4.5A.75.75 0 0 1 8 2Z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        {#- No prefix filter needed on this HTML (unlike MUSASHI's
            prefixHtmlLinks — see .eleventy.js): this template runs
            EleventyHtmlBasePlugin, which rewrites every real href it can
            parse out of the FINAL rendered HTML for pathPrefix, including
            one spliced in here from faq.js via `| safe`. Verified on a
            preview build — filtering it too double-prefixes the link
            (/site/site/#reserve). Links carry no classes of their own;
            styled generically via the wrapper below rather than in the
            data file. -#}
        <div class="mt-4 max-w-none text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-600 [&_a]:text-accent-600 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 [&_a:hover]:text-accent-700 [&_p+p]:mt-3">
          {{ item.answer | safe }}
        </div>
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- FAQPage structured data, generated from the same entries rendered above
    — the visible text and the markup cannot disagree. `about` points at the
    Restaurant node (base.njk) by @id rather than restating name/phone/
    address here: one entity, described once. Worth knowing what this does
    and does not buy: Google narrowed FAQ rich results in 2023 to government
    and health sites, so this will not draw dropdowns in search results. It
    stays because answer engines (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Copilot) parse
    JSON-LD to find clean question/answer pairs — that is the audience this
    block is for.

    `| dump` JSON-encodes each string, quotes included, so answer HTML with
    embedded quotes cannot break out and corrupt the document. -#}
<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "@id": {{ (client.domain + page.url + "#faq") | dump | safe }},
    "mainEntityOfPage": {{ (client.domain + page.url) | dump | safe }},
    "about": { "@id": {{ (client.domain + "/#restaurant") | dump | safe }} },
    "mainEntity": [
      {% for item in faq %}
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": {{ item.question | dump | safe }},
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": {{ item.answer | dump | safe }}
        }
      }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    ]
  }
</script>
{% endif %}
